    {
      "id": "HCAP-11",
      "name": "client-induced NFSv4.1 client expiry recovery",
      "purpose": "Let lane client0 lapse into a courtesy client by partitioning itself past the NFSv4 lease, have client1 open the file client0 holds a write delegation on so the server expires client0, and drive protocol-valid NFSv4.1 recovery",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {
        "syz_calls": [
          "syz_nfs_lane_link$heal_client0",
          "syz_nfs_lane_link$partition_client0",
          "syz_open_nlm_lane_file"
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        "single NFSv4.1 fixture with SERVER_IMPL=both and the default 10 s NFSv4 lease",
        "every trigger is an NFS client action: client0 partitions only its own link in its lane network namespace, and the expiry is the server's reaction to client1's conflicting open; nothing acts on the server namespace",
        "sequence: r0 = syz_open_nfs_lane_profile$client0_knfsd_v41(0x2, 0x0); r1 = syz_open_nlm_lane_file(r0, name, 0x2) (read-write: the server gives client0 a write delegation); syz_nfs_lane_link$partition_client0(0x0, 0x0) exactly once (client0's link silently drops everything it sends for 15 s, past the lease, and the call returns with it still dropping); r2 = syz_open_nfs_lane_profile$client1_knfsd_v41(0x2, 0x1); r3 = syz_open_nlm_lane_file(r2, the same name, 0x2); syz_nfs_lane_link$heal_client0(0x0, 0x1) exactly once; then at least one parser-proven client0-origin NFS I/O operation (statx or getdents64 on r0, not close or lseek)",
        "no client0-origin call between partition and heal: a client0 request then waits on the dead link",
        "knfsd gives no delegation on a file whose delegation it recalled in the last 30 to 60 s, so a repeated program must start from a file it creates: the validated stimulus opens with O_CREAT (mode 0x2) and ends with client0's unlinkat of the file",
        "lane file names are lock0, lock1, lock2 and shared/fixture; client0 and client1 must name the same file, which the parser cannot prove, so a program that names different files only misses the path",
        "the validated run observes nfsd_break_deleg_cb in client1's OPEN request recalling client0's delegation, the courtesy client0 expired and purged by the laundromat, client1's OPEN granted, then client0's EXCHANGE_ID and CREATE_SESSION; the laundromat expiry itself runs in a workqueue and is not attributed",
        "the Stage 1 collector raises the syzkaller program budget (syz-execprog -program-timeout) for a program that partitions, so the 15 s hold and the recovery finish inside one program",
        "validated on lane 0 with one proc (the Stage 1 collector): a Stage 2 manager with more procs does not enable the calls only this capability admits"
      ],
      "status": "validated",
      "scope": [
        "client0_courtesy_expiry_recovery"
      ],
      "source_refs": [
        "bundle/patches/syzkaller/0032-*",
        "bundle/lane/lane.sh",
        "tools/nfs-lifecycle/run.py"
      ],
      "validated_layout": {
        "procs": 1,
        "lanes": [
          0
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "HCAP-13",
      "name": "NLM lane locking and raw NLM RPC",
      "purpose": "Drive the lane knfsd lockd through kernel NFS client byte-range locks and raw NLM calls on the nlm-knfsd NFSv3 fixture",
      "usable_stage": [
        "stage1"
      ],
      "usable_by": [
        "agent_stage1"
      ],
      "interface": {
        "syz_calls": [
          "fcntl$lock",
          "recvfrom$inet_nlm_tcp",
          "syz_nlm_lane_fh",
          "syz_open_nlm_lane_file",
          "syz_send_nlm_rpc",
          "syz_socket_connect_nlm$client0",
          "syz_socket_connect_nlm$client1"
        ]
      },
      "constraints": [
        "nlm-knfsd fixture only: the single NFSv3 knfsd lane with SERVER_IMPL=both, rpcbind and rpc.statd in every lane namespace, both knfsd mounts locking and lockd on TCP port 4045",
        "lock files: r1 = syz_open_nlm_lane_file(r0, name, mode) beneath a knfsd-v3 lane fd (names lock0, lock1, lock2, shared/fixture; mode 0 read-only, 1 read-write, 2 read-write and create), then fcntl$lock(r1, 0x5 F_GETLK or 0x6 F_SETLK, flock); F_SETLKW and OFD locks are never admitted because the collector runs one non-threaded program",
        "raw NLM: r3 = syz_socket_connect_nlm$client0(0x0) or $client1(0x1), then syz_send_nlm_rpc(r3, rpc_nlm_call, len) with exact len fields; the @lane file handle takes r2 = syz_nlm_lane_fh(r0, name) of an existing lane file; read each reply with recvfrom$inet_nlm_tcp before the next call; rpc_nlm_call covers every NLM procedure on version 4 (nlm4) and versions 1/3 (nlm3): null, test, lock, cancel, unlock, granted, the *_msg and *_res forms, and on versions 3 and 4 also share and unshare (nlm_shareargs: cookie, nlm_share {caller, @lane fh, owner, mode, access}, reclaim), nm_lock and free_all (nlm_notify: name, state), so share, unshare, nm_lock and free_all need no new call or constructor",
        "raw NLM share and unshare syz text (share as run in the HCAP-13 KVM campaign): r2 = syz_nlm_lane_fh(r0, &(0x7f0000000040)='lock1\\x00'), r3 = syz_socket_connect_nlm$client0(0x0), then syz_send_nlm_rpc(r3, &(0x7f0000001000)=@v4={0x4, 0x0, 0x2, 0x186b5, 0x4, @share={0x14, @sys={0x1, 0x20, {0x0, {0x9, 'syzkaller'}, 0x0, 0x0, 0x0, []}}, @none={0x0, 0x0}, {@empty=0x0, {{0x9, 'syzkaller'}, @lane={0x14, 0x1000101, 0x0, r2, 0x0}, {0x4, \"01020304\"}, 0x0, 0x1}, 0x0}}}, 0x88); unshare is the same with @unshare={0x15, ...}; NLM version 3 is @v3={xid, 0x0, 0x2, 0x186b5, 0x3, ...} with the same bodies",
        "raw NLM free_all syz text (procedure 23, nlm_notify {caller name, state}): syz_send_nlm_rpc(r3, &(0x7f0000001000)=@v3={0x6, 0x0, 0x2, 0x186b5, 0x3, @free_all={0x17, @sys={0x1, 0x20, {0x0, {0x9, 'syzkaller'}, 0x0, 0x0, 0x0, []}}, @none={0x0, 0x0}, {{0x9, 'syzkaller'}, 0x0}}}, 0x5c); @v4={..., 0x4, @free_all={...}} is the same on version 4; the parser recomputes msglen",
        "attributed: the server lane lockd serving a TCP or UDP NLM request and the client lane lockd serving a callback are context request; the server lockd thread granting a blocked lock and the rpciod steps of the GRANTED_MSG callback and of *_RES replies are context lockd, owned by the program whose LOCK created the block or whose request sent the reply; a grant after that program ended is not attributed; async UNLOCK/CANCEL that the kernel NFS client sends from a syscall run in rpciod unattributed; no Stage 1 call sends UDP NLM",
        "validated on lane 0 with one proc (the Stage 1 collector): a Stage 2 manager with more procs does not enable the calls only this capability admits"
      ],
      "status": "validated",
      "scope": [
        "nlm_lane_lock_rpc"
      ],
